; Qt colors, from the shell's palette: a qt5ct / qt6ct color scheme.
;
; Written by matugen from the current wallpaper - do not edit: change
; matugen/qt-colors.conf.template in olShell instead.
;
; Each list has one color per QPalette role, in the roles' order:
; WindowText, Button, Light, Midlight, Dark, Mid, Text, BrightText,
; ButtonText, Base, Window, Shadow, Highlight, HighlightedText, Link,
; LinkVisited, AlternateBase, NoRole, ToolTipBase, ToolTipText, PlaceholderText
; (qt6ct gives Qt 6.6's Accent the Highlight color). Inactive windows keep the
; active colors; disabled widgets get the secondary text and a plain widget
; background as their selection.

